@page
@model ShopWeb.Pages.TermsModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms & conditions";
}

<h1>Terms &amp; conditions</h1>

<p><em>Silk &amp; Loom OEM scarf studio - effective January 2026</em></p>

<h2>Orders and pricing</h2>
<p>All prices are in US dollars and exclude taxes unless noted. We reserve the right to cancel
and fully refund orders placed at an incorrect price. An order is a binding purchase offer;
acceptance occurs when payment is captured and your order status becomes <strong>Paid</strong>.</p>

<h2>OEM and wholesale terms</h2>
<p>Custom OEM productions (private-label scarf runs) require a signed specification sheet and
a 50% deposit. Lead times and minimums are quoted per run and are not returnable once weaving
has started, except for defects in workmanship.</p>

<h2>Payment</h2>
<p>Card payments are processed by Stripe; PayPal is also accepted. We never store card numbers.
Refunds are issued to the original payment method within 5-10 business days of return approval.</p>

<h2>Returns</h2>
<p>Unused, unworn items in original packaging may be returned within 30 days of delivery.
Custom and monogrammed pieces are final sale. Start a return from your
<a asp-page="/OrderStatus">order status page</a>.</p>

<h2>Intellectual property</h2>
<p>Site content, product photography, and designs are the property of Silk &amp; Loom and its
 licensors. Client-supplied artwork remains the client's property; we retain the right to
 display finished pieces in our portfolio unless NDA applies.</p>

<h2>Governing law</h2>
<p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of New York, without regard to conflict-
of-law principles.</p>
